    "author": "Adam Nichols",
    "category": "Compliance & Legal",
    "content": "## Understanding the Wet DBA in 2026\n\nThe Dutch Tax Authority (Belastingdienst) has resumed strict enforcement of the Deregulation Assessment of Labor Relations Act (Wet DBA). For companies hiring self-employed professionals (ZZP'ers), avoiding 'schijnzelfstandigheid' (bogus self-employment) is no longer optional.\n\n### Key Audit Criteria:\n1. **Authority and Direction:** Does the client have managerial authority over how the specialist works?\n2. **Substitution:** Can the ZZP specialist freely send a qualified replacement without client pre-approval?\n3. **Remuneration and Independence:** Are market rates paid, and does the contractor maintain multiple business engagements?\n\n### How Macee Protects Clients:\nMacee provides DBA-proof model contracts, conducts quarterly risk assessments, and acts as the protective compliance link.",
